---
import Circle from "@free-fall/design-system/components/AttributeCircle.svelte";
import CharacterCircleDemo from "../components/CharacterCircleDemo.svelte";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import "../styles/character-sheet-print.css";
---
<BaseLayout title="Attribute Circle — FREE//FALL Design System">
  <h1>Attribute Circle</h1>
  <p>Current and Base are independent. The attached activation button spends one Current. Base never limits Current.</p>
  <CharacterCircleDemo kind="single" client:load />
  <h2>Static attributes</h2>
  <div class="examples">
    <Circle type="body" current={13} base={12} />
    <Circle type="mind" current={0} base={10} />
    <Circle type="ghost" current={null} base={null} />
  </div>
  <h2>Use in a sheet</h2>
  <p>Import <code>AttributeCircle.svelte</code> from the design-system components. Supply <code>type</code>, <code>current</code>, and <code>base</code>. Static rendering is the default.</p>
  <pre><code>{`<AttributeCircle type="ghost" {current} {base} interactive
  oncurrentchange={(next) => { current = next; }} />`}</code></pre>
  <p>A Svelte parent accepts a proposal by updating the prop synchronously. Keeping the previous value declines it. External prop updates emit no proposals. Use <code>null</code> for an empty field, and <code>appearance="print"</code> for an explicit monochrome specimen.</p>
  <p>The attribute label uses uppercase IBM Plex Mono at <code>--freefall-type-ui-small</code> (0.875rem). Set <code>labelPosition="above"</code> (the default) or <code>labelPosition="below"</code>: its 1.75rem label area is reserved only on that side, with a 0.5rem gap from the face.</p>
  <p><code>--freefall-attribute-circle-width</code> defaults to 11.25rem including the button overhang. The face is 9.875rem across (158px at a 16px root size), close to the circles in the full-size BMG composition. The action uses the shared DS button style and <code>--freefall-button-height</code>: 2.75rem square, with a Material Symbols Sharp bolt icon.</p>
  <p>The face uses <code>--freefall-bg-surface-1</code>, extending 0.1875rem beyond the outline without adding layout space. At the default size, the elevated backing is 164px across. The outline, divider, and button borders use <code>--freefall-border-strong</code>; the circle outline and divider are 0.1875rem (3px) thick. Print uses a plain white face with black lines.</p>
  <p>Hover, press, keyboard focus, and conversion highlighting add a 1px stat-color line in the middle of the 3px circle outline and divider, and bring the background to elevation 2. Entry uses 0.12s ease-in; exit uses 0.4s ease-out. Reduced motion switches immediately; print stays monochrome.</p>
  <p><a href="/bmg-circle/">Compose all three attributes</a> · <a href="/character-sheet-static/">Static and print examples</a></p>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .examples { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--freefall-space-4); }
  pre { white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
</style>
